{'sentiment score': -1, 'confidence': 0.98, 'reason': 'This document provides an overview of the standardized measurement of discounted future net cash flows relating to proved oil and gas reserves. The calculation involves the discount rate, the present value of future cash inflows, and the initial investment in drilling operations. The formula is as follows: (PVIF) = Σ [(FV x P/F, n)] x Discount Rate where PVIF is the present value of an annuity, FV is the future value, P/F is the present value factor, and n is the number of years in the period. The accretion of discount is calculated by subtracting the initial investment from the discounted future net cash flows. The accretion of discount is then added to the discounted future net cash flows. The standardized measure of discounted future net cash flows relating to proved oil and gas reserves represents the sum of the accretions of discounts for each period.', 'company_name': 'COMPANY CONFORMED NAME:\t\t\tENERGY RESOURCES 12, L.P.'}